    "body": "**M5 took this PR over** (the user asked for it; claim on #1614 at 16:10Z). New head `5f22d9d5`: one merge of `upstream/main` (389fe96c) and one fix commit. No rebase, no force-push. The PR stays a draft for the quick pass.\n\nWhat the merge resolved:\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps`, the state block: `clearZ` (this PR) and `afterAsk` / `setupNext` (#1650, #1532) are all kept. No logic conflict: #1650 does not change the first-traverse code.\n- Four Tormach contour goldens (#1577 climb): main's side taken, then regenerated with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`. All 32 moved goldens differ from main by exactly one `G0 Z..` line before the first X/Y traverse.\n- `tests/common/legacy_program.rs`: identical on both sides (#1632 and #1636), merged clean. `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`: merged clean, Tormach bullet kept.\n- The tester-kit `.camproj`, which the earlier `WRITE_GOLDEN` run re-saved (format only), is back to main's file.\n\nFix commit: a refused first traverse now writes no motion. Before, the post wrote the combined `G0 X20 Y10 Z2` after the warning. This is the same rule as NeoTech's review of #1636. The refusal pin asserts this, and a mutation check confirmed it. The decision file now has a \"Taken on trust\" record (the clearance plane over the tool-change X/Y).\n\nThe 03:38Z Hub run shows no problem in this PR's motion. The G30 dip is #1626 and is not in this PR.\n\nGate: post suites ok, clippy clean. App suites are green except `lead_approach`, which fails on main too (#1675).\n",
